  "narrative": {
    "text": "**Business & market dynamics:** First Watch’s rapid unit expansion is driving strong top-line growth, with record new restaurant openings broadening its geographic footprint. However, the same-restaurant sales narrative is softening; traffic has turned negative, pressured by weather disruptions and broader industry headwinds aimed at casual dining. Menu updates and digital initiatives are helping sustain positive comps, but the mix of robust new-store contributions and cautious same-store traffic trends is prompting analysts to trim fair-value estimates, reflecting a more guarded view of near-term demand resilience.\n\n**Management strategy and execution:** Management is executing an aggressive growth plan, achieving record restaurant openings while actively refreshing menus and expanding marketing to protect traffic. Operational discipline is evident in improving restaurant-level margins through favorable menu mix and expense leverage. Leadership attributes recent traffic softness largely to transitory weather, maintaining a steady hand on the unit expansion strategy. The market’s reaction suggests credibility in the long-term store economics remains intact, though the near-term guidance posture is being viewed with increased caution as execution must now navigate a more selective consumer environment.",
